### Direct call to the mock payment gateway (same request the REST Connector sends)
POST http://localhost:8090/payments/api/v1/charges
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ORD-2001

< ./payment-charge.request.json

### Declined token
POST http://localhost:8090/payments/api/v1/charges
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ORD-9999

{"orderId": "ORD-9999", "amount": 100, "currency": "INR", "paymentToken": "tok_test_card_declined", "customerRef": "CUST-9999"}

### Start an order through the lab app
POST http://localhost:8092/api/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

< ./start-instance.request.json

### Start an order through the Camunda 8 REST API (v2)
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

< ./camunda-rest-create-instance.request.json

### Payment outage on / off
PUT http://localhost:8090/admin/faults/payment?mode=DOWN
###
PUT http://localhost:8090/admin/faults/payment?mode=UP

### Inventory outage inside the job worker on / off
PUT http://localhost:8092/admin/worker-faults/inventory?mode=DOWN
###
PUT http://localhost:8092/admin/worker-faults/inventory?mode=UP

### Live results table
GET http://localhost:8092/api/scenarios/results.md
